Description:
  Installs Solid Queue as the Active Job backend with configuration
  and Procfile.dev integration.

  Adds the gem, creates a config file, configures the application
  to use Solid Queue, and updates Procfile.dev.

  When maquina:mcp is installed (app/models/mcp/tools.rb exists), it also
  writes app/models/mcp/tools/solid_queue.rb, MCP tools visible only to users
  on the backstage list (User#backstage_access?): queue_status, list_failed_jobs and get_failed_job (arguments
  redacted by app/agents/error_redactor.rb, copied when missing). They are
  read-only. With --mcp-write the file also gets retry_failed_job and
  discard_failed_job, write tools that need a token with the write scope. An existing tool file is
  never overwritten. Without maquina:mcp nothing MCP-related is written;
  running maquina:mcp later installs the read-only tools.

Examples:
  rails g maquina:solid_queue

  rails g maquina:solid_queue --database postgresql

  rails g maquina:solid_queue --mcp-write
